WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.209 --> 00:00:13.234
[Subtitles by danielsangeo]

00:00:15.125 --> 00:00:18.577
Okay, accident or not, I've killed
so many people at this point,

00:00:18.577 --> 00:00:20.945
I have to be changing
the course of history.

00:00:20.945 --> 00:00:24.811
I've mostly been killing soldiers, though,
and they're not as likely to change history

00:00:24.811 --> 00:00:26.923
unless it's a really decisive battle.

00:00:26.923 --> 00:00:31.063
Or maybe if they're smart and go on to
do important things later in life, but...

00:00:31.063 --> 00:00:33.877
no, there's no risk of that.

00:00:33.877 --> 00:00:35.861
I haven't killed any smart ones.

00:00:35.861 --> 00:00:38.200
Okay, is this really locked solid?

00:00:40.191 --> 00:00:42.615
No, I think these joints are loose.

00:00:42.615 --> 00:00:46.100
Yeah, yeah, I just have to work
this here. I can pry it open.

00:00:46.605 --> 00:00:47.507
Waah!

00:00:47.507 --> 00:00:49.934
There's a reason that door's locked!

00:00:52.119 --> 00:00:54.601
Fucking... bees? Is that all
this is?

00:00:58.301 --> 00:01:00.868
I'M NOT ALLERGIC TO BEES, ASSHOLES!

00:01:03.620 --> 00:01:06.465
And they die on impact;
they don't even swarm.

00:01:06.465 --> 00:01:09.402
Are they toxic? I don't think so.

00:01:09.402 --> 00:01:12.531
Earth bees are more
hardcore than space bees.

00:01:12.531 --> 00:01:14.569
I guess the conventional wisdom is true.

00:01:14.569 --> 00:01:16.004
[vortigaunt charging]

00:01:16.004 --> 00:01:16.549
[shudder]

00:01:16.549 --> 00:01:18.539
OKAY, EVERYBODY SETTLE DOWN!

00:01:18.539 --> 00:01:18.968
[shudder]

00:01:21.390 --> 00:01:21.968
[shudder]

00:01:23.024 --> 00:01:24.300
DID YOU SAY SOMETHING?!

00:01:27.176 --> 00:01:28.634
YOU NEED TO SPEAK UP!

00:01:32.934 --> 00:01:33.500
[shudder]

00:01:35.607 --> 00:01:36.200
WHAT?!

00:01:37.493 --> 00:01:38.033
[shudder]

00:01:41.093 --> 00:01:42.334
I CAN'T HEAR YOU!

00:01:43.667 --> 00:01:44.300
[shudder]

00:01:46.373 --> 00:01:49.100
YOU WANT ME TO SHOOT YOU?!
SURE, I CAN DO THAT!

00:01:50.620 --> 00:01:51.567
IS THAT ENOUGH?!

00:01:53.146 --> 00:01:54.634
OKAY, I'LL KEEP IT COMING!

00:01:56.564 --> 00:01:58.367
HOW ABOUT NOW?! IS THAT GOOD?!

00:01:59.256 --> 00:02:00.000
HELLO?!

00:02:02.336 --> 00:02:04.012
Yeah, I think that's good.

00:02:04.012 --> 00:02:05.934
They would let me know if
there was a problem.

00:02:07.099 --> 00:02:11.834
Well, I've gotta say, the soldiers picked
the right spot for building a gunner's nest.

00:02:11.834 --> 00:02:14.951
I'm starting to think the
teleportation isn't so random.

00:02:14.951 --> 00:02:17.592
I don't know, it's just a hunch I have.

00:02:17.592 --> 00:02:20.368
Jesus, how many was that?
Twenty?

00:02:20.368 --> 00:02:23.731
Well, it's a total waste. We need to be
moving in here with rubber suits

00:02:23.731 --> 00:02:26.022
and hooking these guys up
to a power plant.

00:02:26.022 --> 00:02:29.646
Maybe I can come back here and
capture one; use it to power a cabin.

00:02:29.646 --> 00:02:32.286
I could really live off the grid then.

00:02:32.286 --> 00:02:34.619
Okay, this way's not happening.

00:02:34.619 --> 00:02:37.603
Hey, what is this pink...
volcano anyway?

00:02:37.603 --> 00:02:39.868
It looks like the asphalt has cancer.

00:02:40.818 --> 00:02:44.667
Okay, good. That means that
the Earth... isn't... alive.

00:02:45.723 --> 00:02:46.400
OH GOD!

00:02:46.589 --> 00:02:51.526
[screaming]

00:02:51.526 --> 00:02:53.133
[whimpering]

00:02:54.785 --> 00:02:55.474
NO!

00:02:55.474 --> 00:02:57.188
I'M NOT A LOTTO BALL!

00:02:57.188 --> 00:03:00.327
THE LAST TIME I GOT JUGGLED
THROUGH THE AIR, IT WAS HORRIBLE!

00:03:00.327 --> 00:03:02.771
YOU'RE THE REASON WE HAVE NAPALM!

00:03:02.771 --> 00:03:05.711
THERE'S NO EXCUSE FOR BEING WHAT YOU ARE!

00:03:05.711 --> 00:03:07.300
[machine gun fire, Xenian attack sounds]
Oh no...

00:03:08.475 --> 00:03:11.985
Oh, they're fighting each other!

00:03:11.985 --> 00:03:13.500
Wow...

00:03:14.097 --> 00:03:17.484
This must be, what, the second time now?

00:03:17.484 --> 00:03:20.086
Y'know, maybe it's even the third.

00:03:20.086 --> 00:03:21.667
And bullets win again.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:22.834
Who would've thought?

00:03:24.531 --> 00:03:27.071
Hey, you're the winner! You won!

00:03:27.071 --> 00:03:28.801
[machine gun fire]
Oh!

00:03:30.030 --> 00:03:32.349
And you, too! It was a team effort!

00:03:32.349 --> 00:03:34.297
Everybody wins!

00:03:34.297 --> 00:03:35.968
Especially me.

00:03:37.462 --> 00:03:40.932
Hey, I just realized, if a soldier
assassinated somebody important,

00:03:40.932 --> 00:03:43.000
they could also change the
timeline that way.

00:03:43.541 --> 00:03:45.075
But, if they can't get past me,

00:03:45.075 --> 00:03:48.778
can they really get past
Secret Service or private security?

00:03:48.778 --> 00:03:51.300
Their targets won't be
blaze-orange like me.

00:03:52.793 --> 00:03:56.373
But, does the universe really
care about our timeline, anyway?

00:03:56.373 --> 00:03:59.052
I think we're giving ourselves a
bit much credit here.

00:03:59.052 --> 00:04:00.505
[snarks chirp]
Shit...

00:04:00.505 --> 00:04:02.367
Gah! GOD!

00:04:03.114 --> 00:04:04.400
Well, maybe...

00:04:04.774 --> 00:04:07.794
If Booth hadn't shot Lincoln,
this might not be happening.

00:04:07.794 --> 00:04:10.070
[snarks chirp]
No! NO! No...

00:04:10.070 --> 00:04:14.514
So, uh, case in point, since we
know extraterrestrial life now,

00:04:14.514 --> 00:04:17.999
that means, statistically, there's
probably billions of worlds with life.

00:04:17.999 --> 00:04:20.337
So, we could blow up our own
planet on this timeline

00:04:20.337 --> 00:04:22.834
and the universe doesn't really care.

00:04:23.427 --> 00:04:25.103
HECU: Sir, I hear something...

00:04:25.103 --> 00:04:26.801
I spaced out again, didn't I?

00:04:28.570 --> 00:04:29.300
[whimpering]

00:04:31.019 --> 00:04:31.576
Hey, how are ya doing?

00:04:31.576 --> 00:04:32.306
I'm from Maintenance?

00:04:32.306 --> 00:04:34.400
I heard you're having some trouble
with the ventilation in here?

00:04:35.602 --> 00:04:36.200
HECU: MOVE IN!

00:04:38.515 --> 00:04:41.202
I don't think they believed me.

00:04:41.202 --> 00:04:42.769
Well, it's hard to think of excuses

00:04:42.769 --> 00:04:45.914
when people are shooting at
you inside a ventilation shaft.

00:04:45.914 --> 00:04:48.067
I had the same problem in high school.

00:04:49.387 --> 00:04:50.053
[rocket-propelled grenade launch]

00:04:50.053 --> 00:04:50.797
[gasp]

00:04:51.185 --> 00:04:51.901
HECU: SQUAD...!

00:04:52.532 --> 00:04:53.500
[explosion]

00:04:54.327 --> 00:04:54.834
HECU: Medic!

00:04:57.740 --> 00:04:59.222
[explosions]

00:04:59.222 --> 00:05:00.320
[gasping]

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:01.951
Holy crap!

00:05:01.951 --> 00:05:03.750
What the fuck just happened there?

00:05:03.750 --> 00:05:07.340
I opened the door and they tossed
in the explosives immediately--

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:10.528
before they even saw me,
especially with the sun outside.

00:05:10.528 --> 00:05:13.454
How did they know I wasn't a
wounded soldier exiting?

00:05:13.454 --> 00:05:15.327
I guess they just didn't give a shit,

00:05:15.327 --> 00:05:18.619
which seems to be the answer to
everything the military does.

00:05:18.619 --> 00:05:19.200
Hey, does this--

00:05:20.092 --> 00:05:21.734
It's just a big button!

00:05:22.471 --> 00:05:23.567
Step right up!

00:05:24.058 --> 00:05:25.534
This is amazing!

00:05:27.015 --> 00:05:27.701
WOW!

00:05:29.064 --> 00:05:32.787
Okay, guys, I think that's enough; I don't
know how many shells are in this thing.

00:05:32.787 --> 00:05:35.141
Okay, so we have some more dead people.

00:05:35.141 --> 00:05:38.103
But, we've established that I can
murder an unlimited number of people

00:05:38.103 --> 00:05:40.964
and the universe won't be
affected in any measurable way.

00:05:40.964 --> 00:05:44.937
I'm definitely affecting the human
timeline, though, but again, how much?

00:05:44.937 --> 00:05:47.983
Because, say one of these guys
will invent a... quantum communicator,

00:05:47.983 --> 00:05:51.109
and I just shot him, was he
really our only hope?

00:05:51.109 --> 00:05:53.957
In terms of probability, won't
some other guy in Australia

00:05:53.957 --> 00:05:56.599
just invent a quantum
communicator three years later?

00:05:56.599 --> 00:06:00.010
[soldiers, Xenians attacking]
Oh, good. Good, good, good, good, good.

00:06:00.010 --> 00:06:02.204
Carry on; I'm just an impartial observer.

00:06:02.204 --> 00:06:03.655
Pretend I'm not even here.

00:06:03.655 --> 00:06:06.094
I'm very impressed with how
things are proceeding.

00:06:06.094 --> 00:06:08.290
I'll have good things to say
in my report.

00:06:08.290 --> 00:06:10.367
HEY, I SAID PRETEND I'M NOT EVEN HERE!

00:06:10.964 --> 00:06:13.160
Okay, well this guy's going to
cost you a few points,

00:06:13.160 --> 00:06:15.067
but other than that, very high marks.

00:06:15.698 --> 00:06:16.300
When I file the--

00:06:18.125 --> 00:06:20.200
Hey, you're late.
You think I don't see that?

00:06:23.956 --> 00:06:25.434
This is going in my report.

00:06:26.919 --> 00:06:30.755
There! I punched your timecard
for you. Now, get back to work.

00:06:30.755 --> 00:06:33.486
Maybe I'm not as impartial
as I think I am.

00:06:33.486 --> 00:06:35.201
Wait a minute; I have to be!

00:06:35.201 --> 00:06:37.198
I don't even know what's going on!

00:06:37.198 --> 00:06:41.197
Y'know, for this not being my fight,
an awful lot of people want to kill me.

00:06:41.197 --> 00:06:45.413
Or, not just me, everybody wants
to kill everybody, except me wanting to--

00:06:45.413 --> 00:06:46.133
ah, fuck it.

00:06:50.002 --> 00:06:51.334
I'm so confused.

00:06:52.450 --> 00:06:56.749
This is kind of like shotgun chess where
I need to kill them in the right order.

00:06:56.749 --> 00:06:57.434
Or else...

00:06:59.208 --> 00:07:00.584
See, I did it wrong.

00:07:02.306 --> 00:07:03.234
Okay, check...

00:07:05.699 --> 00:07:07.534
Dammit, I didn't see the bishop.

00:07:10.312 --> 00:07:11.434
I don't like chess.

00:07:16.006 --> 00:07:19.604
See, the problem with chess is it all comes
down to who can think more moves ahead,

00:07:19.604 --> 00:07:20.958
and not in a clever way.

00:07:20.958 --> 00:07:22.977
You could be Einstein or Tesla,

00:07:22.977 --> 00:07:26.278
but you're always going to lose to that
psycho who memorizes board positions

00:07:26.278 --> 00:07:28.300
and can remember fifty moves in his head.

00:07:28.936 --> 00:07:29.567
Waaahh...

00:07:30.789 --> 00:07:35.090
Computers can beat us in chess because
it's a game meant for computers.

00:07:35.090 --> 00:07:38.166
I don't like games that are about
who can memorize the most crap,

00:07:38.166 --> 00:07:39.642
because that's what it is.

00:07:39.642 --> 00:07:42.450
It's not like memorizing
chemical bonds in the periodic table,

00:07:42.450 --> 00:07:44.781
which has a shitload of applications.

00:07:44.781 --> 00:07:49.255
Memorizing chess plays are only about
moving pieces around to feel smug about it.

00:07:49.255 --> 00:07:51.767
Hm, I guess that's why it's so popular.

00:07:52.602 --> 00:07:56.267
Well, speaking of stalemates, I'm kind of
undecided about who to be shooting here.

00:07:57.018 --> 00:07:57.400
Oh!

00:07:58.904 --> 00:08:00.100
Besides you!

00:08:00.811 --> 00:08:01.634
No...

00:08:02.302 --> 00:08:06.121
Because, let's face it, I want the
soldiers and aliens to just kill each other.

00:08:06.121 --> 00:08:08.428
Or, more specifically,
stop shooting me.

00:08:08.428 --> 00:08:09.545
Now, if I had to choose,

00:08:09.545 --> 00:08:13.322
the knee-jerk reaction would be I want
the soldiers to win, but do I really?

00:08:13.322 --> 00:08:13.998
[lock jiggles]

00:08:13.998 --> 00:08:16.855
The aliens mostly just bees
and electric shocks,

00:08:16.855 --> 00:08:20.877
and while that's really fucking annoying
and painful, it's not bullets.

00:08:20.877 --> 00:08:24.473
Plus, if the soldiers win, I
still lose; I'm a fugitive.

00:08:24.473 --> 00:08:26.281
Okay, I don't know where I'm going.

00:08:26.281 --> 00:08:27.508
Uhh...

00:08:27.508 --> 00:08:30.445
Okay, I guess I'm going to have
consort with the dark powers here

00:08:30.445 --> 00:08:31.701
because I'm out of ideas.

00:08:32.151 --> 00:08:33.300
[screaming]

00:08:34.030 --> 00:08:36.901
Okay, thank you, O Dark Ones.
I pay homage.

00:08:37.553 --> 00:08:38.934
Now, where's that straggler?

00:08:39.453 --> 00:08:42.434
He's upsetting the delicate
balance of not being dead.

00:08:43.494 --> 00:08:45.868
Yep, more bees. Yep.

00:08:47.878 --> 00:08:50.267
You think you're the scariest
person that's followed me?!

00:08:53.217 --> 00:08:53.868
Raahh...

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.434
Okay, here, I have an idea:

00:08:57.833 --> 00:08:59.501
Why don't you go and take a look at--

00:08:59.501 --> 00:09:02.649
Shit. No, don't look at that.
That's...

00:09:09.094 --> 00:09:11.693
Well, I can't just walk away;
he's seen me.

00:09:11.693 --> 00:09:13.451
That means I'm going to wake up
three days from now

00:09:13.451 --> 00:09:15.701
with him standing over me in my motel room.

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:18.186
Nnnyaaah...

00:09:18.186 --> 00:09:20.715
There, that should give him
something to think about.

00:09:20.715 --> 00:09:24.646
Yeah, see, if the aliens win, not only
will the charges against me be forgotten,

00:09:24.646 --> 00:09:26.238
but they're not too bright.

00:09:26.238 --> 00:09:29.779
Their most devastating weapon is
being able to teleport anywhere,

00:09:29.779 --> 00:09:32.801
and they're not using that
anywhere near its potential.

00:09:35.973 --> 00:09:37.200
What is this?

00:09:41.984 --> 00:09:44.687
So, this weird tunnel goes to
something f--

00:09:44.687 --> 00:09:45.801
Uhh...

00:09:46.337 --> 00:09:47.300
Aaah-ha-ha...

00:09:47.802 --> 00:09:48.592
[explosion]

00:09:48.592 --> 00:09:49.148
[screaming]

00:09:49.148 --> 00:09:54.167
[underwater mumbling, loud rumbling]

00:09:56.380 --> 00:09:57.367
[gasping]

00:09:57.367 --> 00:09:59.033
Oh, okay.

00:09:59.356 --> 00:10:01.754
I refuse to believe that
is the only purpose

00:10:01.754 --> 00:10:04.500
of this horizontal pipe with a small pool.

00:10:05.518 --> 00:10:06.497
[lock jiggles]

00:10:06.497 --> 00:10:09.167
Oh... shit...

00:10:11.800 --> 00:10:12.968
HECU: Check in, people.

00:10:14.394 --> 00:10:16.400
Oh... man...

00:10:19.237 --> 00:10:22.868
HECU: Recon in position, all quiet.

00:10:23.441 --> 00:10:26.834
Well, at least they didn't tell me
to put that in my pipe and smoke it.

